    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a condensed lineup, as core speed threats like **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Trea Turner**, and the burgeoning **Caleb Durbin** are unavailable due to scheduled off-days. Consequently, we are relying on **Christian Yelich** and **Junior Caminero** to carry the offensive load against tough pitching. **Christian Yelich** earns the highest score of the day at 53.93; while he faces a difficult matchup against Rasmussen, his dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed starter and his prime position in the #3 hole provide the stability needed to anchor our lineup. **Junior Caminero** follows closely at 53.53, benefiting from a favorable #4 batting order spot, though his ceiling is suppressed by a challenging matchup against Henderson.\n\nGiven the thin roster availability, the bench decision process was largely dictated by the calendar rather than performance metrics. **Yordan Alvarez** was the most notable exclusion, sitting purely because of the team-wide rest day. While **Yelich** and **Caminero** both hover in the \"Marginal\" range of our 40\u201359 scoring tier, they represent our most viable path to production. With our speed specialists\u2014**Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Trea Turner**, and **Caleb Durbin**\u2014all sidelined, we lack the stolen base upside that typically defines our strategy, making today a defensive effort to maintain our cumulative category standing. We are monitoring **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** closely, but as no additional games are scheduled, the roster remains locked in its current configuration. Caution is advised as we navigate these two starts without the backup of our high-floor speed contributors.",
